        "original_id": "d372f8eb-92bf-5fb5-8770-c41598f44b9f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: New York Islanders, New York Rangers, Pittsburgh Penguins, New Jersey Devils, New York Knicks, New York Liberty, National Hockey League, National Basketball Association, WNBA\n- Places: New York metropolitan area, Madison Square Garden\n- Events: 1974–75 New York Islanders season playoffs\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1974–75 New York Islanders season playoffs, the New York Islanders defeated the New York Rangers in three games in the first round.\n- In the 1974–75 New York Islanders season playoffs, the New York Islanders then defeated the Pittsburgh Penguins in seven games in the Quarter-finals after losing the first three games.\n- The New York Rangers are one of three National Hockey League franchises in the New York metropolitan area, along with the New Jersey Devils and the New York Islanders.\n- Madison Square Garden is the home arena of the New York Rangers of the National Hockey League, the New York Knicks of the National Basketball Association, and, since 1997, the New York Liberty of the WNBA.",
